raygui for generated9

The original immediate-mode controls, styles and embedded icons, compiled
as a native library on top of raylib. No new window system or event loop.
See UPSTREAM and LICENSE for the pinned source and local changes.

After installing libraylib:

    cd /sys/src/libraygui
    mk install

Clients include u.h, libc.h, raylib.h and raygui.h, and compile with -p.
The header selects the library. Do not define RAYGUI_IMPLEMENTATION in a
client: the implementation is already in libraygui.a.

Call the controls between BeginDrawing and EndDrawing in a rio window.
The caller owns widget state and layout; raygui uses raylib's input queue.
modelview(1) is a complete client with a text box, buttons, check boxes,
slider and status bar. See raygui(2) for a small example.

Native regression test, inside a rio window with VirGL available:

    cd /sys/src/libraygui/test
    mk test

The test checks rendered styles, several queued UTF-8 characters in one
frame, capacity limits, Unicode backspace and clipboard insertion, and
color-picker interaction.
Only amd64/QEMU VirGL has been tested. Rendering and font limitations are
those of raylib(2); this is not a replacement for native rio applications.
